WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.625
If you want to understand machine learning, start with K-means.

2
00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:04.447
Each dot marks a house's location.

3
00:00:04.641 --> 00:00:06.504
Choose three groups, so K is three.

4
00:00:06.676 --> 00:00:08.266
K-means picks three starting centers.

5
00:00:08.529 --> 00:00:11.230
This dot is closest to purple, so it joins that group.

6
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.988
Now every dot picks its nearest center.

7
00:00:13.166 --> 00:00:15.158
Orange's center is off to one side.

8
00:00:15.158 --> 00:00:18.078
Average the dots' positions left to right, then up and down.

9
00:00:18.078 --> 00:00:19.488
Every dot counts equally.

10
00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:21.969
Those two averages give the new center: the mean.

11
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.696
Do this for every group.

12
00:00:23.871 --> 00:00:26.969
Now the centers have moved, so a dot might be closer to a different one.

13
00:00:26.969 --> 00:00:29.910
Check every dot again, update the groups, then move the centers again.

14
00:00:30.108 --> 00:00:32.024
Keep repeating until the groups stop changing.

15
00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:35.494
That's K-means: assign, average, and repeat until the groups settle.

